ah what's in the box  [Music]  so this is kind of a long overdue  follow-up to I think the most viewed  video that I have which was my five  things that dark boone needs to stop  doing and my number one on that was  mystery boxes which to reiterate what  that is it's the it's the the question  that gets seated across the series that  we get an answer to at the end so in  series one it was bad wolf series - it  was Torchwood series three it was Harold  Saxon series four it was rose you know  showing up at the very beginning and  then a couple of other points across it  Sears five the crack series six good old  eyepatch lady kept showing up see seven  kind of only did one for a half but that  was of course Clara with the impossible  girl thing series eight who is busy  series nine what is the hybrid series  ten was in the vault  etc etc so that's what they have been up  to this point now more than a few people  and commented on that video telling me  that they like the mystery boxes but  then pretty much all of them explain why  and they weren't actually defending the  mystery boxes they were defending the  concepts of season arcs and they're not  the same thing so a season arc is  whatever the connective tissue is that  is you know being the through line  running throughout the episodes of the  of the season of the series now mystery  boxes is how dr. who has chosen to -  season arcs up to this point that is by  no means the only way to do a season arc  and that was kind of the point I tried  to make and I guess didn't make as  clearly as I could have I don't have a  problem with season art I like season  arcs I'm a problem with the fact that  the show up to this point has been doing  the exact same style of season arc over  and over and over again it doesn't help  that the whole nature of the mystery box  thing is something that kind of wears on  me in general because I get irritated  when it's very obvious that you're just  dangling something that you are going to  withhold information from us for a while  and there are exceptions like I do think  say the cracks in time were one of the  better ones because they actually  impacted the story as it went along as  opposed to just something that got said  randomly to remind you that it's a thing  until we find out what it is which is  how the vast majority of these have  worked heck I think even Martha was  getting sick of them by the end because  even though I do think that the vault  and you know what's in the vault counts  as a mystery box for series 10 they wrap  that up even before we got to the finale  so he even he was kind of just do it in  an obligatory way but coming back to  what I said before this is not the only  way to do season arcs there are a  multitude of ways of doing season arcs  so that's what I'm sick of I'm sick of  this method of doing it of course I want  connective tissue and I am but at the  same time I still like that most  episodes are more or less standalone I  don't want Doctor Who to become  massively serialized where it's just one  or two stories told over the 13 episodes  where you see an episode and it's not a  complete thing you have to see the next  two three four five entire season worth  whatever I don't want it to turn into  that I don't want it to become Breaking  Bad I don't want it to become  broadchurch I like talk to - tell me a  more or less complete story in one  occasionally two episodes but it is nice  to have something that is something we  keep coming back to that can keep us  moving along so what are some options  aside from a mystery box well there's  the Buffy the Vampire Slayer approach ie  The Big Bad which is to have the thing  that is connecting the episodes that we  keep coming back to and the thing that  we know is going on in the background be  a villain a villain that we touch back  on a villain with plans a villain who we  see move those plans forward maybe they  are interacting directly in the story of  a given episode maybe we just  touch on them a little bit to remind you  that they are up to something that is  gonna have to be dealt with and no not  revealing what the villains plan that  does not make it a mystery box because  what's connecting everything is the  villain and the threat as opposed to the  mystery of exactly what it is they're  gonna be trying to pull it off so you  can have a mystery aspect to that and  it's not gonna literally be as much of a  retread has don't you want to find out  what this is which is what the mystery  box always is so that's one way to do  that you can do that with any number of  villains in a way I suppose they kind of  did that with Missy but really only in  hindsight when you go back and look at  series 8 again because we didn't know  who that she was we didn't know she was  good news bad news or just some weird  nebulous thing that with its own agenda  that was neither inherently good or evil  you get to the end you find out who she  is and then it kind of becomes a big bad  story but first viewing it was a mystery  box another option if you just want to  go more subtle and not have a blatant  piece of connective tissue just have the  progression from episode to episode be  character focused have it be character  journeys how what they went through last  time affected them and how it's changing  them a little bit every episode and we  watched the journey of a character we  got a little bit of this with Capaldi's  era with various characters they did it  a bit with Clara and series 9 but  completely botched the ending of that  hell bent and I've said before that I  feel like the doctor himself went  through a journey and is a changed  character from series 8 to 9 to 10 but  in a lot of ways it feels like that was  a transition that happened between  series first when he's very grumpy  second when he's kind of overdoing  trying to be cool it's almost like a  lend life crisis and then in his third  series he's kind of settled into a  basically a good healthy place or as  good and healthy as he can be for as  much damage as he has but we don't  really and we see the things that he  experiences so we understand why he's  different from what he was last time we  saw him but we don't actually see that  for him it just kind of you have to kind  of just assume that it happened because  the start of every series he's a little  bit different into his his intro every  time he feels like a little bit of a  different character and Wow  I do still maintain that that did feel  like a proper arc for his character and  not just inconsistent writing at least I  don't feel it did it still could have  been done as a stronger clear through  line for here's the way that this  character is changing and it does not  necessarily have to be him it can be a  campaign which I said they kind of tried  to do with Clara and 9 and I mainly  didn't stick the landing but up to that  point it was kind of working with you  know the whole her getting cockier and  trying to be like him and then  ultimately that getting her killed they  kind of did it there but then they  completely undermined it later on plus  they were giving us a mystery box on top  of that anyway with the stupid hybrid  thing so I don't know what Chibnall is  up to none of us do we can speculate I'm  sure a lot of people are speculating  that it it could be a more serious  approach but I think that's mainly just  based on the fact that he did  broadchurch which was very serialized  and I don't think that's an automatic  given it could go a number of ways on  that but if we are going to do  connective tissue and through lines for  a series from episode to episode or  things that we are following bead that  stretch beyond whatever the individual  episodes story is can't just not be a  whew don't you want to find out what  this thing is again just please I need a  break however else you want to do it I'm  open to finding out but just just give  me one series of about it please so  those are my thoughts on trying to  clarify what I mean when I say please no  more mystery boxes what are your  thoughts on all this whatever they are  drop something down the comments and  let's talk about it and there's all that  stuff that you can do you know the stuff  likes and subscribes and patreon support  maybe by t-shirt follow me on Twitter  listen to my podcast links for all that  stuff is it down in the description and  until next time  this council is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

